● The Open Society Foundations (OSF), founded by George Soros, has invested over $32
billion in human rights and social justice causes since its inception.
○ In Eastern Europe, OSF-funded projects have strengthened press freedom,
provided legal support for asylum seekers, and enabled local NGOs to monitor
government abuses.
○ In 2019, OSF provided $220 million to organisations working on racial justice in the
U.S., reinforcing movements that aim to dismantle systemic discrimination.
● The Ford Foundation has similarly committed substantial resources to human rights
causes, including $1 billion in grants for initiatives on gender equality, economic justice, and
civil rights across Latin America, Africa, and Asia.
○ For example, its funding in Latin America has supported indigenous rights in the
Amazon, and it has empowered local communities to combat land grabs and
environmental exploitation.
● By backing these causes, foundations like OSF and Ford have amplified global human
rights advocacy, enabling sustained efforts to challenge inequality and injustice in even the
most difficult environments.
